{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cfa2d175a000759e","name":"Laser Trip Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-cfa2d175a000759e","title":"Laser Trip Mine","revision":19510,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:06:13Z","sha256":"3aa1d5cb9a03392aff97c2428f318ea60689620b3f2797b81a300ac5070f576e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19510","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Laser%20Trip%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cfa2d175a000759e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 700\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.5 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mines, unlike traditional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosives"},", are designed to be placed in the ground or otherwise hidden from sight. Anyone attempting to notice a Mine takes a -5 penalty on his or her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check. Setting a Mine is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," that does not require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check. However, attaching a detonator (either a Timer or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manual Trigger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manual_Trigger","referenceId":"reference:3bac33a88449a688"},") requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check as usual, and supersedes the Mine's normal triggering system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Often used in high-security areas or in places where security is more important than the preservation of the structure, Laser Trip Mines use a nearly invisible laser beam that acts as a tripwire to detonate the Mine. A Laser Trip Mine is placed on the ground (in any square adjacent to you) or against any other solid surface; you then designate a single solid surface within 6 squares as the laser's terminus. The Laser Trip Mine is triggered when any character, creature, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," enters a square that is part of the line between the square where the Laser Trip Mine is placed and the square that is the laser's terminus. A Laser Trip Mine damages everything in a 2-Square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Tiny\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 6d6 (Energy)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 2-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
